00:00:02.149 --> 00:00:04.340 align:start position:0%
originally owned by the daughter of  Marie Antoinette's governess this  chateau is a trove of hidden  architectural gems about 30 miles  outside of Paris stands chateau de  Grasse built in 1815 it remained a  family home until the 1930s when it was  bought by an Italian arts patron who  made modifications including  chinese-inspired gardens the Tartar tent  and a theatre the private mini theater  of chateau de Grasse opened in 1957 and  is inspired by a baroque opera house in  Germany today it is still active with  plays and concerts taking place  throughout the year  one of the chateaus most admired  features is the library it is said that  it was Cecile Payton's inspiration for  the library in the film my fair lady but  the most unusual feature of all is the  Tata  tent a painted metal pavilion but made  to look like a fabric tent the interior  of which features 10,000 Delft tiles the  Chateau was declared a historic monument  in 1993 and is open to the public for  weekend visits or special events a walk  through this Chateau really shows how  the other half lived  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

